                        "content": "A client with a history of type 2 diabetes is admitted to the hospital with chest pain and scheduled for a cardiac catheterization. Which medication would need to be withheld for 24 hours before the procedure and for 48 hours after the procedure?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nMetformin needs to be withheld 24 hours before and for 48 hours after cardiac catheterization because of the injection of contrast medium during the procedure. If the contrast medium affects kidney function, with metformin in the system the client would be at increased risk for lactic acidosis. The medications in the remaining options do not need to be withheld before and after cardiac catheterization.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nEliminate glipizide and repaglinide first because they are comparable or alike. Although these medications may be withheld on the morning of the procedure because of the client's NPO (nothing by mouth) status, there is no indication for withholding the medication on the day prior to the procedure and postprocedure. Regular insulin may be administered if elevated blood glucose levels from infused intravenous solutions occur on the day of the procedure.",
                        "id": "00cd6c861ce948168d1297d1a1ea3835",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "5d191b73ff6c4f95a05710b02807b1da",
                                "content": "With food"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "084ae73927f54e81a5abe8c0b7b52e8e",
                                "content": "At lunchtime"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "6bc90132984546e49b1e5eb96dc4f4b4",
                                "content": "On an empty stomach"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f26ecd5b43eb482cbf85ea4d06696b0e",
                                "content": "At bedtime with a snack"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
