                        "content": "Potassium iodide is prescribed for a client with thyrotoxic crisis. The client calls a clinic nurse and complains of a brassy taste in the mouth. Which instruction would the nurse provide the client?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nChronic ingestion of iodine can produce iodism. The client needs to be instructed about the symptoms of iodism, which include a brassy taste, soreness of gums and teeth, vomiting, and abdominal pain. The client needs to be instructed to notify the PHCP if these symptoms occur.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, that the client is experiencing a brassy taste. Eliminate options 2 and 4 because the nurse cannot legally alter medication prescriptions without the PHCP's prescription. Focusing on the client's symptom presented in the question will eliminate option 1, to continue with the medication.",
                        "id": "038afbbf6cb844ad8a136290f046b5ef",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f05f7b92f1ef4a37a5021929ceebb9ba",
                                "content": "\"Sulfonylureas decrease insulin resistance.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "df80e5ed1df048d09ea3ea2668915d7f",
                                "content": "\"Sulfonylureas inhibit carbohydrate digestion.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "68a0bb356a004cc7a00024e7dd53a458",
                                "content": "\"Sulfonylureas decrease glucose production by the liver.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "52b60dd4c8194f1f8ecea8f3ff99f5f1",
                                "content": "\"Sulfonylureas promote insulin secretion by the pancreas.\""
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "f05f7b92f1ef4a37a5021929ceebb9ba",
                                    "content": "\"Sulfonylureas decrease insulin resistance.\""
                                },
