                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The diabetes nurse specialist conducts a teaching session to a group of nursing students regarding sulfonylureas, oral hypoglycemic medications used for type 2 diabetes mellitus. Which statement, describing the primary action of these medications, would the nurse include in the teaching session?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nSulfonylureas promote insulin secretion by the pancreas and may also increase tissue response to insulin. Thiazolidinediones decrease insulin resistance. α-Glucosidase inhibitors inhibit carbohydrate digestion. Biguanides decrease glucose production by the liver.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nNote the strategic word, primary. Knowledge of the specific action of sulfonylureas is required to answer this question. Remember that sulfonylureas promote insulin secretion by the pancreas.",
                        "id": "04bdcdc0ab37498c87f44c5cd391ac03",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "cacd02ccf1ef4d5f99b5d2cc59fce8e8",
                                "content": "Insulin glargine"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "42dafcbd1d77436aa9eb62e03e737adb",
                                "content": "Regular insulin"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
