                        "type": "0",
                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "The emergency department nurse is caring for a client admitted with diabetic ketoacidosis. The physician prescribes intravenous (IV) insulin. The nurse plans to prepare which type of insulin for the client?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nRegular insulin can be administered by the IV route. Insulin glargine is a long-acting insulin. Insulin isophane and 50% human insulin isophane/50% human insulin are intermediate-acting insulins.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nFocus on the subject, insulin that can be administered by the IV route. To answer correctly, it is necessary to remember the onset, peak, and duration of action of each insulin type. Also, focus on the client's diagnosis, and recall that the blood glucose level is extremely elevated in this condition and must be decreased.",
                        "id": "06c3b0252d994a1fadaefdecdef9d359",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "1bff4351e0844228bc9b66c6b2466144",
                                "content": "Carbamazepine and phenytoin by mouth"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "37bd23f5c1c34dcda02a869a31e46d6e",
                                "content": "Lioresal by mouth and diazepam intravenously"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "ee6544b86af1471bb91fd41e0f24dfc1",
                                "content": "Phenytoin intravenously, then tapered to oral route"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "1257b2bcf98f48ffa14d677dea216132",
                                "content": "Methylprednisolone and cyclophosphamide intravenously"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "1bff4351e0844228bc9b66c6b2466144",
                                    "content": "Carbamazepine and phenytoin by mouth"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "37bd23f5c1c34dcda02a869a31e46d6e",
                                    "content": "Lioresal by mouth and diazepam intravenously"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "ee6544b86af1471bb91fd41e0f24dfc1",
                                    "content": "Phenytoin intravenously, then tapered to oral route"
                                },
