                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nDesmopressin is an antidiuretic hormone (ADH) used in the treatment of diabetes insipidus. It promotes renal conservation of water by acting on the collecting ducts of the kidney to increase the permeability to water, which results in increased water reabsorption. Desmopressin does not relieve headaches, stimulate aldosterone, or decrease production of ADH.\n\nTest-Taking Strategy:\nNote the subject, the purpose of desmopressin, and the diagnosis identified in the question. Recalling the pathophysiology and the clinical manifestations associated with the disorder will assist in directing you to the correct option.",
